{"type":"event","v":1,"turnId":"bff7e976-e1a0-48f7-a662-858ac850d90a","index":82,"at":1794327612981,"event":{"type":"tool_result","agent":"general","name":"toolRequest","callId":"call_tool_request_1","content":"{\"enabled\":[\"timeNow\",\"actionRequest\",\"threadFork\",\"toolManage\",\"toolRegistry\"],\"tools\":[{\"name\":\"timeNow\",\"description\":\"Read the current time. Returns an ISO 8601 timestamp and the Unix time in seconds. The timezone argument is only a label for the answer.\",\"tags\":[\"time\",\"clock\",\"date\"]},{\"name\":\"actionRequest\",\"description\":\"Ask the owner a bounded question when the request is genuinely ambiguous and guessing would be unsafe or wasteful. Supply ONE question, 2-8 distinct options (each an id plus a short label and optional description), and `recommended` set to the id of the option you suggest. The owner may still answer with free text, so never assume your recommendation was accepted; the tool result tells you exactly which answer was chosen. Ask at most one focused question at a time, and never use this for a decision you can make safely yourself.\",\"tags\":[\"question\",\"ask\",\"clarify\",\"owner\",\"user\",\"choice\",\"interaction\"]},{\"name\":\"threadFork\",\"description\":\"Fork a private thread that reads the ENTIRE current conversation independently and returns one final summary. Use it when a self-contained investigation benefits from isolated reasoning without polluting this transcript. The new thread cannot see later messages and never receives this agent's tools automatically beyond the runtime grant. Pass the task as `input`; `label` is an optional short display name. The fork shares this process and any external side effects, so it is not a sandbox.\",\"tags\":[\"fork\",\"thread\",\"branch\",\"history\",\"summarize\",\"research\"]},{\"name\":\"toolManage\",\"description\":\"Inspect and edit registered tools. `list` returns registry metadata, `details` inspects one tool, `source` returns its captured module text and local dependencies, `path` resolves a tool source path or a candidate path inside the configured toolFolders, `create` and `update` register a module and, by default, persist it: `create` writes a safe `<name>.tool.ts` filename in the LAST configured toolFolders entry, and `update` rewrites the tool's owning source path (an explicit `path` overrides either). Set `persist: \\\"runtime\\\"` to opt out of disk writes explicitly; that mode keeps the module in this session's registry only and cannot be combined with `path` or `folder`. `reload` recompiles the installed source revision. Every mutation is validated and published atomically through the same kernel as toolCreate/toolRegistry; a failed compile leaves the previous tool registered. Loaded tool code runs with this process's full permissions - there is no sandbox.\",\"tags\":[\"tools\",\"manage\",\"source\",\"edit\",\"reload\"]},{\"name\":\"toolRegistry\",\"description\":\"Compile and register a tool from editable source, replacing any existing registration with the same name. Provide `sourcePath` (a tool-source-relative or absolute path) or `moduleText` (full TypeScript/JavaScript module text). The module must export a Tool (named/default), a `tool` export, or `metadata` + `execute`. Local helper imports are compiled from source; `node:` imports and package dependencies resolve through Node. Success returns the installed name and source revision and makes the tool immediately callable; syntax, loading, or contract failures return diagnostics and leave the previous registration untouched. Transpilation checks syntax, NOT semantic types or runtime correctness, and loaded code runs with full process permissions.\",\"tags\":[\"tools\",\"registry\",\"source\",\"self-modifying\",\"compile\"]}],\"matched\":5,\"omitted\":0}","isError":false,"outcome":"completed","durationMs":1,"thread":{"id":"1"}}}
